<urn:atm:triage:finding/S12-QA1-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "S12-QA1-004" ;
  triage:title "sprint-S12.md describes INTG-RSH-003 incorrectly — wrong finding attributed to that ID" ;
  triage:description "docs/phase-S/sprint-S12.md:53: The sprint doc describes INTG-RSH-003 as 'Pre-existing reconcile_runtime shutdown race — document intentional deferral if out of scope, otherwise apply same bounded-shutdown pattern.' The canonical triage record (INTG-RSH-003.ttl) defines it as 'No PATH_MAX ceiling on tilde-expanded hook paths' in crates/atm-core/src/config/discovery.rs:66. These are completely different findings. Sprint-S12.md designates triage records as canonical (line 70). The sprint doc description of INTG-RSH-003 is incorrect and creates confusion about what was required. Fix: correct sprint-S12.md line 53 to describe the canonical finding: 'crates/atm-core/src/config/discovery.rs:66 — No PATH_MAX ceiling on tilde-expanded hook paths (CONFIRMED SATISFIED on integrate/phase-S base; verify still present at bd9e0e8).'" ;
  triage:category "DOC" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
